meta {
  name: Delete Write Request
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/write-requests/{{writeRequestId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  Permanently removes the request and its activity timeline. Only the requester (or an admin) can, and only a DRAFT / CANCELLED / REJECTED / FAILED / EXECUTED request — a PENDING one is someone else's review queue and an APPROVED one may be mid-execution, so cancel those first (409 otherwise).

  The `audit_log` entries it wrote (WRITE_SUBMIT, WRITE_EXECUTE, …) live in their own table and survive, so deleting tidies the queue without erasing the record that a change was proposed or run. A `WRITE_DELETE` entry is added.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}).
}
